          "topic": "Explain the application of immunohistochemistry (IHC) and special stains in tumor diagnosis.",
          "generatedNotes": "**Role of Immunohistochemistry (IHC) in Tumor Diagnosis**\n\n- IHC uses specific *antibodies* to identify cell products or surface markers that are not visible through standard *hematoxylin and eosin (H&E)* staining.\n- It is essential for determining the *lineage* of tumors that appear morphologically similar but require different treatments.\n\n**Categorization of Undifferentiated Malignant Neoplasms**\n\n- Many anaplastic tumors (carcinomas, lymphomas, melanomas, and sarcomas) look identical under a microscope. \n- IHC identifies specific *intermediate filaments* and *membrane proteins* to distinguish these origins:\n\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th>Marker Type</th>\n      <th>Specific Marker</th>\n      <th>Diagnostic Target</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>Intermediate Filament</td>\n      <td>*Cytokeratins*</td>\n      <td>Epithelial origin (*Carcinoma*)</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>Intermediate Filament</td>\n      <td>*Desmin*</td>\n      <td>Muscle cell origin (*Sarcoma*)</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>Membrane Protein</td>\n      <td>*CD20*</td>\n      <td>*B-cell Lymphomas*</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Identification of Primary Site in Metastatic Disease**\n\n- When a patient presents with a metastasis of unknown origin, IHC is used to detect *organ-specific antigens*:\n- *Prostate-specific antigen (PSA)* &rarr; Identifies metastatic *Prostatic Adenocarcinoma*.\n- *Thyroglobulin* &rarr; Identifies metastatic *Thyroid Carcinoma*.\n\n**Prognostic and Therapeutic Applications**\n\n- IHC identifies molecules that determine the specific therapy a patient should receive:\n- *Estrogen/Progesterone Receptors (ER/PR)*: Detected in breast cancer; presence indicates susceptibility to *antiestrogen therapy*.\n- *HER2 (ERBB2)*: Overexpression in breast cancer indicates a poor prognosis but identifies candidates for *anti-HER2 antibody* therapy.\n- *ALK Protein*: Presence in lung cancers or lymphomas indicates the use of *tyrosine kinase inhibitors*.\n\n**Diagnostic Logic Pathway**\n\nUndifferentiated Tumor Biopsy &rarr; Initial IHC Panel (*Cytokeratin*, *Desmin*, *CD20*) &rarr; Determination of Lineage (e.g., Epithelial vs. Lymphoid) &rarr; Targeted Organ-Specific IHC (*PSA*, *Thyroglobulin*) &rarr; Identification of Primary Site/Therapeutic Targets (*HER2*, *ER/PR*).\n\n**No relevant information found in the provided text regarding specific \"special stains\" (e.g., PAS, GMS, or Mucin stains) beyond standard histologic and IHC methods.**"
